course: dictionary
lesson: 15532
title: Adding endings with suffixes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A suffix is a group of letters added to the end of a word. Adding one can make a new word. «Kind» plus «-ness» makes «kindness», and «hope» plus «-ful» makes «hopeful». Adding a suffix to a word is called suffixation.
explain: Suffixation can change what kind of word you have. «Kind» is an adjective, but «kindness» is a noun, a thing you can name. «Quick» becomes «quickly» when you add «-ly», and then it tells you how something is done.
explain: Sometimes the spelling changes too. «Happy» becomes «happiness» when the y changes to i. «Run» becomes «running» when you double the n. Check the spelling rule before you add the ending.
fact: Suffixation means making a new word or a new form of a word by adding a suffix to the end.
fact: A suffix is a word ending such as -ness, -ful, -ly, -ed or -s.
fact: «Kind» + «-ness» = «kindness». «Hope» + «-ful» = «hopeful». «Quick» + «-ly» = «quickly».
fact: Suffixation can change the word class: an adjective like «kind» can become a noun like «kindness».
fact: Spelling can change too: «happy» becomes «happiness», and «run» becomes «running».
exercise: Which suffix turns «kind» into «kindness»? | -ly | -ed | -ful | *-ness
exercise: Which word is made by adding -ful to «hope»? | *hopeful | hopeless | hopes | hoped
exercise: «She ran quickly to school.» The word «quickly» comes from «quick». Which suffix was added? | -ness | -ed | -ful | *-ly
test: What is suffixation? | Taking the first letters off a word | *Adding a word ending, such as -ness or -ful, to a word to make a new word or form | Writing a word backwards
test: Which word is a noun made from «happy» with a suffix? | happied | happily | *happiness | happyful
exam: Which is the correct spelling of «run» with -ing added? | *running | runned | runing | runnning
